WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Thursday,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.400
the twelfth of November. This
episode is written and read with AI.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.240
Gulf crude exports are back near
four-fifths of pre-war levels,

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.320
but refined products are lagging
badly, and US diesel futures jumped

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.160
as Iran denied holding
talks with Washington.

6
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.960
In Europe, Poland's Orlen has become
the first buyer to walk away from

7
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.400
a long-term Qatari gas contract.

8
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.440
On the markets. Brent was up nearly
three percent at ninety-three dollars

9
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.533
ninety a barrel late on
Wednesday morning in New York,

10
00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.440
according to OilPrice dot com.

11
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.333
West Texas Intermediate was
near eighty-eight dollars,

12
00:00:37.387 --> 00:00:41.893
and heating oil, the US diesel
benchmark, rose four point one percent.

13
00:00:41.947 --> 00:00:45.640
In Europe, front-month gas at the
Dutch Title Transfer Facility,

14
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.400
or TTF, rose two point seven percent
to about eighty-seven euros a megawatt

15
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.800
hour. EU gas storage stood at seventy-one
point six percent on the tenth

16
00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.880
of November, according to
Gas Infrastructure Europe.

17
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.200
The Gulf's recovery is lopsided.

18
00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.240
According to FGE, Middle
East crude exports,

19
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.200
pipeline barrels included, are back
to about eighty to eighty-five percent

20
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:12.213
of pre-war levels. Refined products are
stuck at around thirty-five percent.

21
00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:15.600
Producers are moving crude first
and holding back products while the

22
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.867
strait stays vulnerable. That keeps
diesel and jet fuel from Jubail,

23
00:01:19.893 --> 00:01:23.720
Ruwais and Al-Zour scarce,
even as crude loosens.

24
00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.800
It's why heating oil
outran Brent on Wednesday.

25
00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.413
Refiners with access to
crude pick up margin,

26
00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:33.160
while importers who leaned on Gulf
product cargoes are paying more.

27
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.720
The crude side is clearly coming back.

28
00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.920
Saudi Arabia told OPEC it produced just
under ten point six million barrels

29
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.040
a day in October. That's up
twenty-six percent from September.

30
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.613
It's the kingdom's highest
output since February,

31
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:49.960
and slightly above its quota of
about ten and a half million.

32
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.827
Riyadh put supply to the
market, net of storage,

33
00:01:52.853 --> 00:01:55.560
at about nine point two
million barrels a day.

34
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.800
If crude keeps outrunning products,
diesel margins could widen further.

35
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.560
Turning to gas. Orlen has terminated
its long-term contract with QatarEnergy

36
00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.400
for one million tonnes
of liquefied natural gas,

37
00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.627
or LNG, a year. In a regulatory
filing late on Tuesday,

38
00:02:11.653 --> 00:02:15.440
the Polish company cited the supplier's
inability to deliver under force

39
00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.280
majeure.

40
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.440
The deal dates from two thousand nine.

41
00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.680
Deliveries began in twenty sixteen and
were due to run to twenty thirty-four.

42
00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.320
Orlen is the first long-term
Qatari customer to cancel,

43
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.600
and there's no reported
response yet from QatarEnergy.

44
00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.160
It lands in a tight European market.

45
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.040
Storage slipped about four
tenths of a point on the day,

46
00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.280
and Wednesday's TTF gain came off a
one-month low near eighty-two euros

47
00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.800
earlier in the week. In a note
dated the fourth of November,

48
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.880
Kpler said it expects TTF to head
back toward one hundred euros,

49
00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.360
citing colder weather, lower
Norwegian flows and early withdrawals.

50
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.200
Germany, meanwhile, will go ahead
with a state crisis gas reserve of

51
00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.200
twenty-four terawatt hours after
missing its winter storage targets,

52
00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.720
according to the economy ministry.

53
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.520
Gas users will fund it through surcharges.

54
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.320
Should other long-term
buyers follow Orlen,

55
00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.160
the Qatari volumes freed up later
could end up on the spot market rather

56
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.520
than in legacy contracts.

57
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.520
Back to the Gulf, and the politics
behind Wednesday's oil rebound.

58
00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.640
The move followed a
denial by Mohsen Rezaei,

59
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.040
Iran's top security official, that
Tehran is negotiating with Washington,

60
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.480
OilPrice dot com reported.

61
00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.800
That is Iran's position only.

62
00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.280
The reported Qatari mediation track
remains unconfirmed by either side.

63
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.200
Brent had lost about twenty-one
percent since the start of November on

64
00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.960
bets the war was ending. As of
a note on the fifth of November,

65
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.560
Kpler estimated that trend-following
funds had sold around one hundred

66
00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.520
and twenty-six million
barrels during the slide.

67
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.360
The attacks haven't stopped.

68
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.200
United Kingdom Maritime Trade
Operations reported a tanker struck by

69
00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.680
an unidentified projectile on Tuesday,
nineteen nautical miles northeast

70
00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.280
of the strait. It was one of
two tankers attacked that day.

71
00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.160
Iran claims three vessels hit naval mines,

72
00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.600
Splash twenty-four seven reported,
though owners and flag states have

73
00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:10.160
not confirmed it. As many as thirty-seven
vessels were attacked in October,

74
00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.800
a monthly record, according
to OilPrice dot com.

75
00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:17.280
For shipowners and crews, the risk
on this route is still very live.

76
00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.840
Over in the Baltic, Ukrainian drones
struck the port area of Ust-Luga,

77
00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.640
Russia's Baltic export
hub, early on Wednesday,

78
00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.120
according to the Leningrad
regional governor.

79
00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.040
The strike started a fire, injured
three workers and forced the emergency

80
00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.600
shutdown of a transformer substation.

81
00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.840
That moves Ukraine's campaign from
refineries to export infrastructure.

82
00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.160
It came on the second day of US-led
Russia-Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi,

83
00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:46.240
Rigzone reported. Today's reports
don't show yet whether Baltic loadings

84
00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.200
were interrupted.

85
00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.960
Separately, the Russian diesel tanker
that had been idling off the US

86
00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:55.120
East Coast made a U-turn about four
hundred nautical miles off New York,

87
00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.560
Bloomberg reported. Analysts cited by
gCaptain say US buyers are unlikely

88
00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:04.080
to take Russian diesel, despite
President Trump's temporary sanctions

89
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:04.960
waiver.

90
00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:09.520
On sanctions, Canada has reinstated
measures against the National Iranian

91
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.200
Tanker Company, reversing relief
granted under the nuclear deal,

92
00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.200
according to Splash twenty-four seven.

93
00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:19.360
The package covers eleven entities,
including the National Iranian Oil

94
00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.720
Company and Naftiran Intertrade.

95
00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.840
Kpler said in a note on the second
of November that higher-risk tankers

96
00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.160
are lifting a growing share of Gulf crude.

97
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.200
A few more things.

98
00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.400
The Panama Canal has raised daily
transits to thirty-four and restored

99
00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.080
the Neopanamax draft to fifty
feet after a wet October,

100
00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.600
according to the canal authority.

101
00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.880
That eases routing from the US Gulf to
Asia for LNG and liquefied petroleum

102
00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:45.460
gas.

103
00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.840
ADNOC Gas, part of the Abu
Dhabi National Oil Company,

104
00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:53.360
doubled its third-quarter net income
from the previous quarter to about

105
00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.600
one point three billion dollars.

106
00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.440
It raised its profit guidance for
this year to at least four billion.

107
00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:05.120
ADNOC's ten-year LNG deal with Gujarat
is put at up to four million tonnes.

108
00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.880
US retail gasoline has fallen below
four dollars a gallon for the first

109
00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.000
time since August, according to GasBuddy.

110
00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.440
And the Department of Energy has closed
a four hundred and eighty million

111
00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.600
dollar loan for Arena Energy to
redevelop twenty-two platforms on the

112
00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:24.080
US Gulf shelf. At peak, the project
could add nearly thirty-nine thousand

113
00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.360
barrels a day.

114
00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.080
What to watch next. Daily EU storage
readings run through the eighteenth

115
00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.880
of November, as TTF tests the
hundred-euro level Kpler expects.

116
00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.040
And on the fifteenth, the US emergency
waiver of the Jones Act expires.

117
00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.760
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
